solated Workspaces.Upload PDFs or paste raw research texts/abstracts, which are immediately parsed and analyzed by Gemini to extract key claims, limitations, and entities.Run Multi-Document Synthesis Reports that output structured JSON rendered into rich UI tables, contradiction cards, and evidence-backed decision briefs.Query their workspace corpus via a Contextual Research Assistant that refuses to hallucinate outside the provided sources and cites specific uploaded documents.Export or save synthesized findings into persistent Knowledge Artifacts for downstream reporting.4. Mandatory FeaturesJWT + Bcrypt Authentication System: Complete registration, login, session verification (/api/auth/me), and protected route middleware.Research Workspace Management: Create, read, update, and delete domain-specific workspaces (e.g., Clinical & Biotech, Market & Competitive Intelligence, Public Policy & Legal, Computer Science & AI).Multi-Modal Source Ingestion Pipeline:PDF Upload (Multer): Accept .pdf files up to 10MB, extract raw text server-side using pdf-parse, and immediately trigger Gemini claim/entity extraction.Raw Text / URL Abstract Ingestion: Paste long-form articles, transcripts, or abstracts directly with custom bibliographic metadata (Author, Publication Year, Source Type).AI Source Deconstruction (Auto-Analysis on Ingest): Every ingested source is analyzed by Gemini to generate:Executive SummaryCore Empirical Claims (with strength rating: High, Moderate, Speculative)Key Entities / KeywordsStudy Methodology & Identified LimitationsCross-Source Synthesis & Contradiction Matrix: Users select 2 to 10 sources inside a workspace and choose a Synthesis Mode (Comprehensive Literature Review, Consensus vs. Contradiction Matrix, Research Gap Finder, or Executive Evidence Brief). Gemini outputs a strictly typed JSON report stored in PostgreSQL.Grounded Corpus Q&A Chat: Interactive chat threads per workspace where the backend injects the extracted text and claims of all workspace sources into the Gemini context window, returning answers with explicit source citations (citedSourceIds).Knowledge Graph & Entity Explorer: Visual tag cloud and filterable entity matrix showing which concepts appear across multiple documents in a workspace.Analytics & Research Telemetry Dashboard: High-level KPI metrics (Total Workspaces, Sources Analyzed, Claims Extracted, Contradictions Flagged, Synthesis Reports Generated).5. Technology RequirementsFrontendFramework: React.js (v18+) with ViteRouting: React Router v6 (react-router-dom)Styling: Tailwind CSS + lucide-react iconsHTTP Client: Axios with request/response interceptors for automatic Authorization: Bearer <token> injection and 401 handling.State & Feedback: React Context API for Auth & Active Workspace state, toast notifications for async AI operations.BackendRuntime & Framework: Node.js + Express.js (ES Modules or CommonJS, consistently configured)Authentication: jsonwebtoken (JWT) + bcryptjs (10 salt rounds)Validation: zod for all incoming request bodies, query parameters, and AI JSON response validationFile Handling: multer (memoryStorage) + pdf-parse for extracting text from uploaded PDF documentsSecurity & Utilities: cors, dotenv, helmet, express-rate-limitDatabaseEngine: PostgreSQL (Compatible with Replit Postgres, Neon, Supabase PostgreSQL, or Railway PostgreSQL)Driver: pg (Pool connection using DATABASE_URL environment variable with SSL support when required)Artificial IntelligenceSDK: Official @google/genai SDK (const { GoogleGenAI, Type } = require('@google/genai') or ES import)Model: gemini-2.5-flash for fast, high-context document analysis, structured synthesis, and grounded Q&A.Security Rule: GEMINI_API_KEY must reside strictly in backend .env variables and never be exposed to client bundles.6. Application Pages (Routes)Route PathAccessComponent NamePurpose/PublicLandingPageHero showcase of NexusSynth AI, architecture overview, problem/solution framing, and CTAs to Login/Register./login