SIS, EXECUTIVE_DECISION_BRIEF)focus_directive (Textarea, Optional — Specific angle or hypothesis to test across the selected sources)10. Database Schema (Production SQL for PostgreSQL)Execute this schema initialization automatically on server startup (db/init.js) or via migration script so the app works out-of-the-box:SQLCREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "uuid-ossp";

-- 1. USERS TABLE
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    full_name VARCHAR(120) NOT NULL,
    email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    password_hash TEXT NOT NULL,
    institution VARCHAR(150) DEFAULT 'Independent Researcher',
    primary_domain VARCHAR(50) DEFAULT 'ACADEMIC_SCIENTIFIC',
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 2. RESEARCH WORKSPACES TABLE
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS workspaces (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    title VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL,
    domain VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
    research_question TEXT NOT NULL,
    description TEXT,
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    updated_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 3. RESEARCH SOURCES (INGESTED DOCUMENTS) TABLE
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sources (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    workspace_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workspaces(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    title VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    authors VARCHAR(255) DEFAULT 'Unknown Author',
    publication_year INTEGER,
    source_type VARCHAR(50) DEFAULT 'PEER_REVIEWED_PAPER',
    source_url TEXT,
    file_name VARCHAR(255),
    raw_text TEXT NOT NULL,
    word_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    ai_summary TEXT,
    methodology_notes TEXT,
    limitations TEXT,
    key_claims JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
    entities JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
    key_metrics JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
    analysis_status VARCHAR(30) DEFAULT 'COMPLETED',
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 4. CROSS-SOURCE SYNTHESIS REPORTS TABLE
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS syntheses (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    workspace_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workspaces(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    title VARCHAR(200) NOT NULL,
    synthesis_mode VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
    focus_directive TEXT,
    source_ids JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
    executive_synthesis TEXT NOT NULL,
    consensus_points JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
    contradictions JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
    research_gaps JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
    evidence_matrix JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
    recommendations JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 5. WORKSPACE Q&A CHAT MESSAGES TABLE
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS chat_messages (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    workspace_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workspaces(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    role VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL CHECK (role IN ('user', 'assistant')),
    content TEXT NOT NULL,
    citations JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
    confidence_level VARCHAR(30),
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- PERFORMANCE INDEXES
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_workspaces_user_id ON workspaces(user_id);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_sources_workspace_id ON sources(workspace_id);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_syntheses_workspace_id ON syntheses(workspace_id);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_chat_workspace_id ON chat_messages(workspace_id);
11. Row Level Security (RLS) / Data Isolation RulesEvery database query on protected resources must enforce strict tenant isolation at the SQL query level by binding req.user.id (extracted from the verified JWT):Workspace Isolation: SELECT * FROM workspaces WHERE id = $1 AND user_id = $2Source Isolation: A user can only view, upload, or delete sources belonging to a workspace where workspaces.user_id = req.user.id.Synthesis Verification: When generating a synthesis across source_ids, the backend must query SELECT id, title, authors, publication_year, raw_text, ai_summary, key_claims FROM sources WHERE workspace_id = $1 AND user_id = $2 AND id = ANY($3::uuid[]) to guarantee a user cannot synthesize sources from another user's workspace.Chat History Isolation: All chat queries filter strictly by workspace_id = $1 AND user_id = $2.12. Backend API RoutesAuthentication Routes (/api/auth)POST /api/auth/register — Register a new user, hash password with bcrypt, return JWT + user object.POST /api/auth/login — Authenticate credentials, return JWT + user object.GET /api/auth/me — Verify JWT middleware, return current user profile and aggregate stats.Dashboard & Telemetry Routes (/api/dashboard)GET /api/dashboard/stats — Return total workspaces, total sources, total claims extracted, total synthesis reports, and recent activity feed for req.user.id.Workspace Routes (/api/workspaces)GET /api/workspaces — List all workspaces for req.user.id with source count and synthesis count.POST /api/workspaces — Create a new workspace (Zod validated).GET /api/workspaces/:id — Get workspace details, associated sources list, and synthesis reports list.DELETE /api/workspaces/:id — Delete workspace and cascade delete sources, syntheses, and chats.Source Ingestion & AI Deconstruction Routes (/api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sources)POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sources — Multipart/form-data (multer single 'file') OR JSON body. Extracts PDF text (if file provided) or reads raw_content, runs Gemini Source Deconstruction Prompt, stores source + structured JSON analysis in PostgreSQL, and returns the created record.GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sources/:sourceId — Retrieve full source details including raw_text, key_claims, entities, and methodology_notes.DELETE /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sources/:sourceId — Delete a specific source.Cross-Source Synthesis Routes (/api/workspaces/:workspaceId/syntheses)POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/syntheses — Validate source_ids (min 2), fetch source texts/claims from DB, execute Gemini Cross-Source Synthesis Prompt, save structured synthesis report in syntheses table, and return the report.GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/syntheses/:synthesisId — Get full synthesis report by ID.DELETE /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/syntheses/:synthesisId — Delete a synthesis report.Grounded Knowledge Q&A Routes (/api/workspaces/:workspaceId/chat)GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/chat — Fetch chronological chat history for the workspace.POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/chat — Accept user question, load all workspace sources, execute Gemini Grounded Q&A Prompt, persist both user message and assistant response (with citations) to chat_messages, and return the response.DELETE /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/chat — Clear workspace chat history.13. Gemini SDK Setup & Server-Side SecurityInstall and initialize @google/genai strictly on the backend (server/services/geminiService.js):JavaScriptimport { GoogleGenAI, Type } from "@google/genai";
import dotenv from "dotenv";
dotenv.config();

if (!process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY) {
  console.warn("⚠️ WARNING: GEMINI_API_KEY is not set in environment variables.");
}

const ai = new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY });
